<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 26-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 26-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Peter has strengthened to a typhoon, and is now threatening Okinawa and southern Japan. Peter is under 175 miles south of Okinawa and moving north about 10 mph. Top winds are 85 mph. Peter is expected to have top winds near 100 mph when it passes just west of Okinawa in 12-18 hours. After that, landfall is expected in Kyushu in 24-30 hours, bringing a liklihood of a storm surge and coastal flooding, heavy rain with flash flooding, mudslides in the hilly terrain, and damaging winds, especially in Kyushu.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
